{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772839944,"nonce":"5C0Fxyt6zAH+qqy0hdHDdwS3L+s=","title":"Monitor tab shows \"No active sessions\" despite active session in DB","message":"User reports the Monitor tab (formerly Sessions tab, renamed in feature/rename-sessions-monitor) shows \"No active sessions.\" even though the API confirms an active session exists.\n\n**API evidence:**\n- `GET /api/sessions?include=issues` returns 379 sessions, 1 with status \"active\"\n- `GET /api/sessions/active` returns `{\"error\": \"Session not found\"}` — this is because there is NO route handler for `/api/sessions/active`. The path matches the parameterized `/api/sessions/:id` route, which looks up a session with literal ID \"active\".\n\n**Two issues identified:**\n\n1. **Missing `/api/sessions/active` route:** No explicit route exists in `src/routes/sessions.ts`. If anything relies on this endpoint (CLI, hooks, dashboard), it silently fails. Should add a dedicated handler that returns sessions with status=active.\n\n2. **Monitor tab empty state:** The frontend code in `ui/src/views/sessions.tsx` correctly partitions sessions into active vs dead trees. The API returns correct data. The dashboard fetches `GET /api/sessions?include=issues` on mount. Possible causes: browser cache/JS error, SSE event overwriting state, or a timing issue. Needs browser-side debugging (check console for JS errors, verify localStorage cache state).\n\n**Onset:** ~1 day ago, coinciding with the Monitor tab rename (feature/integrate-console-overhaul merge on 2026-03-05).\n\n**Files involved:**\n- `src/routes/sessions.ts` — missing /active route\n- `ui/src/views/sessions.tsx` — sessions view logic (looks correct)\n- `ui/src/state.ts` — state management (looks correct)\n- `ui/src/app.tsx` — initial fetch + SSE handlers (looks correct)","files":null}]}